      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Looking east from Grafton Road to Carlton Gore Road (foreground), showing the Methodist Church on the corner, built in 1885, and the Sunday School, formerly the church, built in 1866 on Carlton Gore Road (right). In 1927 the church was moved and the Sunday School demolished to make way for the Methodist Collegiate College, built on the site in 1928, later to become the Whitecliffe College of Arts and Design."
